---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="You Found the Still Point"
  description="You're holding one of the coins. Here's what the touchstone in the middle is for, and where to go next if you want more."
>
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-content">
      <span class="coin-face" aria-hidden="true"><span class="coin-stone"></span></span>
      <h1>You found the still point.</h1>
      <p class="epigraph">
        <em>Somebody handed you a coin. Nothing is being asked of you.</em><br>
        <em>This page is just here in case you wanted to know what it was.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="found-content">

    <!-- The object -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>The object</h2>

      <p>Black face, red divot in the middle. The divot is a touchstone — a place for your thumb
      to rest and circle out on the ripples. That's the whole design: something that lives in a
      pocket and gives your hand somewhere to go when your head is going somewhere else. Some of
      them are weighted and some are light; the touchstone works the same either way.</p>

      <p>Everything else is on the back: <strong>find a third way</strong>, and the address that
      brought you here.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- What a still point is -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>What a still point is</h2>

      <p>Everything that turns, turns around a point that holds still.</p>

      <p>You already know several. The top of a breath, before it turns. The beat in a room after
      somebody says something true and nobody rushes to fill it. The half-second between reading the
      message and starting to type.</p>

      <p>It isn't calm. Calm is a mood, and moods can't be scheduled. A still point is just a
      gap — small enough to fit inside five seconds, wide enough to stand in.</p>

      <p>It isn't made, either. It's found. It was in you before the coin was.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- The line -->
    <section class="section">
      <blockquote class="handoff">
        When you're stuck on a binary, one thing or the other, remember to be still, and maybe the
        third way will come to you.
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <!-- The heritage -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>None of this is new</h2>

      <p>Every culture that has ever existed found its own way here. Dervishes spinning until the
      spinning went still. Quakers sitting in silence until the light moved someone to speak. A
      farm kitchen gone quiet for grace. Not one tradition's property — closer to standard human
      equipment, arrived at independently, everywhere, for as long as there have been people.</p>

      <p>Which means nothing was handed to you tonight. You were already carrying this. It just got
      crowded out — there is always something asking for the gap, and lately the things asking are
      very good at it.</p>

      <p>So the coin doesn't supply anything. It reminds. That's the most an object this small could
      honestly claim to do.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- AI disclosure — said plainly, before any invitation -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Said before you go further</h2>

      <p>The stories behind this, and this page itself, are written by a human and an AI working
      together — openly, from the first page, two years now. That's the project: between handing
      your thinking to the machines and refusing them outright, there has to be a third way, and
      the only honest way to look for it is in the open, where you can watch.</p>

      <p>If machine-made things make you wary, you're welcome here — that wariness is earned, and
      nobody will argue you out of it. Just know the coin owes nothing to any of this. The still
      point stands on its own. It was standing before the machines, and it will be standing after.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Where to go -->
    <section class="section next-steps">
      <h2>If you want more</h2>

      <p>There's a project behind the coin, and it started from one stubborn binary: hand your
      thinking over to the machines, or refuse them and be left behind. Neither answer is any good,
      and both were written by people with something to sell. Working out the third one is slow, and
      easier with company.</p>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><a href="/practice">The practice</a> — three units, each one teachable in a breath.
        The first one is already under your thumb.</li>
        <li><a href="https://forum.stillpointproject.org">The forum</a> — somewhere to think out
        loud with other people. It's early: one welcome post, one open room. The first few people
        in help shape what it becomes, which is an honest description and not a sales pitch.</li>
        <li><a href="/stories">The stories</a> — there's fiction here too, near-future, about a
        world that relearns how to be still. Doors into the same question. Free to read.</li>
      </ul>

    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  @import '../styles/design-tokens.css';

  /* Page Header */
  /* Extra top padding so the coin graphic clears the fixed navbar. */
  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: calc(var(--space-3xl) + 3rem) var(--space-lg) var(--space-2xl);
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* The coin, drawn: black face, red stone at the still point. */
  .coin-face {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 4.5rem;
    height: 4.5rem;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #121212;
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1),
      0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }

  .coin-stone {
    width: 1.8rem;
    height: 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #e05a4e, #b23a30);
    box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .epigraph {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.5vw, 1.25rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Main Content */
  .found-content {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .section {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-2xl);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
  }

  .section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section strong {
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .section a {
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* The handoff line — the only thing on this page worth memorising */
  .handoff {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-1);
    padding: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Plain list — matches the practice page */
  .plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .plain-list li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    position: relative;
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .plain-list li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
  }
</style>
